      "title": "What is React?",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "30s",
      "content": "<p>React is a declarative, efficient, and flexible JavaScript library for building user interfaces.</p>\n<p>It lets you compose complex UIs from small and isolated pieces of code called \"components\".</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsx-concept",
      "title": "Understanding JSX",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "45s",
      "content": "<p>JSX is a syntax extension to JavaScript. It is used with React to describe what the UI should look like.</p>\n<pre><code>const element = &lt;h1&gt;Hello, world!&lt;/h1&gt;;</code></pre>"
    },
